			<div class="content" id="post-content-1050497">
									

<p>I dunno. The article as a whole just feels really bare to me, but it's hard to put my finger on <em>why</em>. It felt like it was building up to <em>something,</em> with all these neat little details, but then very few of them are expanded upon any.</p>
<p>*rereads it*</p>
<p>On the other hand, though, the article itself is very straightforward and to-the-point. Adding to it would prolly clutter it. A side-page or two might be interesting, I suppose. Maybe a small-ish experiment log testing the various properties of SCP-210-01 (e.g., can you, say, dip a cup or a bucket in there and lift out some of it? That is, even though it doesn't spill out the windows/doors, can it be "lifted" out? If so, would any of it "lifted" out from the side then spill out in accordance to normal gravity? Does it retain its other properties? If it can be removed, what would happen if you tried to empty it one bucket at a time? What happens if you put a fish or other aquatic animal in there?), or a change log excerpt from the rover.</p>

