			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1050203">
									

<p>I had to reword this line in the description: "The substance possesses a refractory index nearly identical to water which has been dubbed SCP-210-01." Written like that, it looks like you've designated water as SCP-210-01. Now it's much less ambiguous but keeps the same general flow (I think, anyway).</p>
<p>Also, the sentence "SCP-210-02 will not take damage" really bugs me. It sounds like it came from a D&amp;D rulebook instead of an SCP article. I suggest changing that to "Instances of SCP-210-02 cannot be damaged" or somesuch.</p>
<p>All that said, I rather like this one, especially the picture, and I don't think it needs anything more. Graceful, almost delicate, but still plenty dangerous to the unaware.</p>

